DTEND:20261017T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join Horne Creek Farm for our annual Cornshucking Frolic on Sat
 urday\, October 17th\, from 10 am - to 5 pm. The day will highlight histor
 y\, heritage crafts\, music\, and fun!\n\nThe event is sponsored and organ
 ized by the North Carolina Living Historical Farm Committee\, Inc.\n\nAdmi
 ssion fees are as follows:\nAdults: $8.00\, Children 6 - 12: $5.00\, & Chi
 ldren 5 & Under: Free.\n\nHeritage demonstrations and activities are sure 
 to please every member of the family\, from young to old. Quilting\, baske
 t weaving\, knitting\, blacksmithing\, a gristmill demonstration\, log hew
 ing\, information on heirloom apples\, cooking demonstrations\, plowing\, 
 apple butter & sorghum syrup demonstrations\, exhibitions of quilts and an
 tique farm equipment\, plus much more.\n\nNo pets (other than service anim
 als) allowed. No alcoholic beverages allowed.\n\nCanceled in the event of 
 heavy rain.\n\nFor more information: 336-325-2298\n\nHorne Creek Farm Stat
 e Historic Site\n308 Horne Creek Farm Road\nPinnacle\, NC 27043
GEO:36.268201;-80.484677
LOCATION:Horne Creek Living Historical Farm
SUMMARY:Cornshucking Frolic
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/cornshucking-frolic-5674
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
CATEGORIES:Festivals & Fairs
