DTSTAMP:20261017T041252Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53922986344278
DTSTART:20261017T190000Z
DTEND:20261017T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special tour exploring the place of death in the 
 early 1800s. You will walk through the steps of a wake with a trained doce
 nt who will explain to you the community's response to death\, body prepar
 ation\, the wake\, burial and stone cutting techniques. The tour includes 
 a stop in the kitchen house and ends in the cemetery where you will learn 
 the unique history behind the Polk family cemetery.\n\nThis tour is design
 ed to be family friendly and suitable for all ages. All tour fees are paid
  on site prior to the start of the tour.\n\nTour guests can expect up to a
  1/4 mile of walking along some uneven ground. Please wear appropriate sho
 es and clothing for the weather. In the event of extreme heat\, cold or ra
 in\, the tour will be cancelled.
GEO:35.078;-80.882745
LOCATION:President James K. Polk Historic Site
SUMMARY:Death & Dying Seasonal Tour
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/death-dying-seasonal-tour
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Guided Tours
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"NC Cultural Resources": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/spill-the-tea-7522"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/spill-the-tea-7522"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261017T041252Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52507714085620
DTSTART:20261017T190000Z
DTEND:20261017T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:​Spill the Tea! is a bold new musical inspired by the first r
 ecorded act of women's activism in American history — the Edenton Tea Pa
 rty. At the heart of the story is Penelope Barker\, the daring woman who o
 rganized 50 other women to sign a public resolution boycotting British goo
 ds — and sent it directly to King George III. This radical act of defian
 ce\, carried out in a time when women had no political voice\, helped spar
 k a revolution and laid the groundwork\, not only for the birth of a new n
 ation\, but for women to stand up for their rights.\n\nBlending pop\, hip-
 hop\, orchestral\, and classic Broadway musical styles\, Spill the Tea! is
  filled with humor\, heart\, and history. With a witty script plus lavish 
 sets and costumes\, the show celebrates the power of those who refused to 
 stay silent.​
GEO:36.299891;-76.219792
LOCATION:Arts of the Albemarle\, Maguire Theatre
SUMMARY:Spill the Tea!
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/spill-the-tea-7522
CATEGORIES:Performances & Arts
CATEGORIES:Theater & Musicals
END:VEVENT
