DESCRIPTION:Join us at Vance Birthplace on Saturday\, Oct. 17 to get into t
 he spirit of Halloween with spooky stories from Appalachia and beyond! Dr.
  Delanna Reed\, professor emerita of Storytelling at East Tennessee State 
 University\, will bring these tales to life through spoken word from 7pm t
 o 8pm. Visitors are welcome to bring a blanket or chair\, and as the sun s
 ets\, they can take a seat around our campfire. These stories are suitable
  for ages 12 and up.\n\nThis event is free and does not require registrati
 on in advance\, but donations are encouraged. If you have any questions\, 
 please reach out via email at vance@dncr.nc.gov or by phone at (828) 645-6
 706!
GEO:35.700986;-82.496251
LOCATION:Governor Zebulon B. Vance Birthplace
SUMMARY:Frightful Folk Tales at Vance Birthplace
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/frightful-folk-tales-at-vanc
 e-birthplace-1802
