BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_newhopeaudubon
SUMMARY:Chapel Hill Bird Club Bird Outing
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261018T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261018T110000
DTSTAMP:20261017T041320Z
UID:0ni1geo1ofkjdkpa3ce29c51tr@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20261018T080000
SEQUENCE:1
CREATED:20260926T013716Z
DESCRIPTION:Contact Bruce Young at <a href="mailto:byoung715@yahoo.com" t
 arget="_blank">byoung715@yahoo.com</a> for questions. The location will be
  Ebenezer Point\, Jordan Lake. Ebenezer is 2.3 miles south of Hwy. 64 on B
 eaver Creek Road (SR1008) on the east side of Jordan lake. There's a well-
 marked entrance on the right. More information\, including map coordinates
 \, is here: <a href="https://tbg.carolinanature.com/ebenezer.html">https:/
 /tbg.carolinanature.com/ebenezer.html</a><br><br>This outing is sponsored 
 by Chapel Hill Bird Club. More info about this outing is available at:  
 <a href="https://chbc.carolinanature.com/birdwalks/" target="_blank"><u><u
 >https://chbc.carolinanature.com/birdwalks/</u></u></a>.<br><br>Outings us
 ually last 2-3 hours. No reservations or sign-up needed. If there is a lar
 ge turnout for any particular outing\, we may split into two groups. We do
  recommend carpooling for families or friend pods\; while we love pets\, t
 here is a ‘no-pet’ policy for bird outings. New birders and birders of
  all skill levels are welcome. <br><br>Please wear long pants\, socks\, a
 nd sturdy shoes (ticks and chiggers may be present). Sun and bug protectio
 n are also recommended. Bring snacks and water if you like. Heavy rain wil
 l result in cancellation.
LAST-MODIFIED:20261002T235449Z
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:New Hope Bird Alliance
END:VEVENT
