DESCRIPTION:The annual Community Modeling and Analysis System (CMAS) Confer
 ence brings together air-quality researchers\, modelers\, government scien
 tists and environmental professionals from around the world to share advan
 ces in air-quality modeling and its applications. Hosted by UNC-Chapel Hil
 l's Institute for the Environment\, the conference explores emerging resea
 rch\, modeling tools and technologies that help scientists and policymaker
 s better understand air pollution and inform environmental decision-making
 .
