DESCRIPTION:North Carolina and American Independence \n\n \n\nJoin the Univ
 ersity Library and the Department of History for a special exhibition view
 ing and public talk commemorating America's 250th anniversary. Katheen DuV
 al\, Carl W. Ernst Distinguished Professor of History at UNC-Chapel Hill a
 nd recipient of a 2025 Pulitzer Prize for Native Nations: A Millennium in 
 North America\, will share insights into American history. The evening wil
 l include viewing of the Wilson Library exhibition "Witnesses to the Revol
 ution: North Carolina and the War for Independence\,” produced in partne
 rship with the North Carolina Museum of History.\n\n \n\nA book signing wi
 ll follow the talk\; copies of Native Nations will be available for purcha
 se.
LOCATION:Wilson Library\, Fearrington Reading Room
SUMMARY:An evening with historian Kathleen DuVal 
