DTSTAMP:20261017T041253Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54055256254307
DTSTART:20261023T200000Z
DTEND:20261023T223000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join a Ranger to investigate the past at Cabelands. We will hik
 e around 3.5 miles and discuss the history of the area while visiting John
  Cabe's Mill\, an associated homesite\, and the largest known cemetery in 
 Eno River State Park. Be sure to bring your flashlight as the hike will co
 nclude after sunset.\n\nAt least 0.5 miles of hiking is off trail with one
  creek crossing and a fair amount of elevation change. This hike is modera
 te to difficult. All children must be accompanied by an adult. Please be s
 ure to dress appropriately for the weather\, wear hiking shoes\, bring wat
 er\, and a flashlight! It will be dark before the program ends.\n\nSpaces 
 are limited\, and registration is required. To sign up\, call (984) 250-13
 70 or email eno.river@ncparks.gov. Include the number of guests in your pa
 rty and a phone number where you can be reached if the event is changed or
  canceled.
LOCATION:Eno River State Park - Cabelands Access\, Parking Lot
SUMMARY:Ghosts and Gristmills of Cabelands
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/ghosts-and-gristmills-of-cab
 elands
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Outdoor & Recreation
END:VEVENT
