DESCRIPTION:Please join Cricket Crigler\, State Regent of the North Carolin
 a Society of the Daughters of the American Revolution\, and Gloria Halstea
 d\, State Historian\, along with eight sponsoring chapters\, for the dedic
 ation of five commemorative markers honoring the Battle of New Garden on O
 ctober 24 and 25.\n\nSponsoring Chapters:\n\nAlexander Martin ChapterBattl
 e of Alamance ChapterColonel Arthur Forbis ChapterColonel Joseph Winston C
 hapterDeep River ChapterGuilford Battle ChapterRachel Caldwell ChapterWill
 iam Bethell ChapterThe dedication ceremonies are free and open to the publ
 ic. Five markers will be placed commemorating the three engagements that c
 omprise the Battle of New Garden — the engagement in the lane\, the enga
 gement at the meeting house\, and the engagement at the crossroads — as 
 well as the encampments of General Nathanael Greene and General Charles Co
 rnwallis.\n\nRegistration is requested but not required: https://ncsdar.re
 gfox.com/2026-ncsdar-battle-of-new-garden-
LOCATION:Multiple locations see itinerary for details
