BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/teacher-talk-unpacking-american-indian-heritage-month"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261017T041253Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54178528171769
DTSTART:20261028T220000Z
DTEND:20261028T230000Z
DESCRIPTION:Unpacking American Indian Heritage Month\nWed. Oct. 28\, 2026 |
  6:00–7:00 pm (followed by Q&A)\n\nA free virtual discussion for K-12 ed
 ucators \n\nAmerican Indian Heritage Month each November offers a powerful
  chance for educators to highlight the rich cultures\, histories\, and ong
 oing contributions of American Indian communities in North Carolina. In pr
 eparation\, K–12 educators are invited to join DNCR’s NC American Indi
 an Heritage Commission to deepen essential understandings of contemporary 
 American Indian tribes across the state while dispelling common misconcept
 ions and stereotypes. \n\nParticipants will explore practical ideas\, vett
 ed resources\, and culturally grounded approaches that support meaningful 
 integration of Native people\, stories\, and perspectives into classroom i
 nstruction\, during November and throughout the entire school year.\n\nEdu
 cators in attendance can request a .1 CEU form after the event. \n\nDon’
 t miss this opportunity to strengthen your practice and ensure your studen
 ts learn accurate\, relevant\, and inspiring North Carolina Native narrati
 ves all year long.\n\nRegistration\n\nPlease fill out this form no later t
 han Oct. 28 at Noon to register\; a zoom link will be provided via e-mail 
 several days before the event.\n\nQuestions?\nContact education.outreach@d
 ncr.nc.gov \n\nPresenter\nStephen Bell serves as Associate Director of the
  North Carolina American Indian Heritage Commission within the N.C. Depart
 ment of Natural and Cultural Resources (DNCR.) In this role\, he supports 
 statewide initiatives and partnerships that preserve\, interpret\, and cel
 ebrate American Indian history\, arts\, customs\, and culture. Bell has mo
 re than a decade of experience serving students\, educators\, and communit
 ies\, having begun his career as a middle school science teacher and later
  serving as a school social worker and American Indian Education Coordinat
 or for Guilford County Schools. Bell is a citizen of the Lumbee Tribe of N
 orth Carolina. He was named the National Indian Education Association’s 
 National Educator of the Year in 2023 and received the Native American 40 
 Under 40 Award in 2025.\n\nLearn more about the NC American Indian Heritag
 e Commission at aihc.nc.gov. \n\nVisit DNCR’s page featuring our K-12 ed
 ucation resources at dncr.k12.nc.gov.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Teacher Discussion: Unpacking American Indian Heritage Month
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/teacher-talk-unpacking-ameri
 can-indian-heritage-month
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Lectures & Talks
END:VEVENT
