DTSTART:20261029T210000Z
DTEND:20261029T223000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us for Memory & Texture\, a special conversation exploring
  Black hair\, memory\, art and culture.\n\n \n\nJamaica Gilmer\, artist an
 d curator of REVERENCE: Hair Memory Through Images\, will be in conversati
 on with Dr. Jasmine N. Cobb\, author of New Growth: The Art and Texture of
  Black Hair. The conversation will be moderated by Dr. LeRhonda S. Manigau
 lt-Bryant\, director of the Sonja Haynes Stone Center.\n\n \n\nThursday\, 
 Oct. 29\n5 p.m.\nBrown Gallery\, Sonja Haynes Stone Center\nRSVP: https://
 go.unc.edu/ReverenceExhibition\n\n \n\nCome experience an engaging dialogu
 e inspired by the themes of REVERENCE and the powerful ways Black hair car
 ries history\, identity\, memory and meaning.\n\n \n\nJamaica Gilmer’s e
 xhibition\, REVERENCE: Hair Memory Through Images\, is on view at the Ston
 e Center through May 31\, 2027. Be sure to stop by and experience the exhi
 bition!
GEO:35.907852;-79.050272
LOCATION:The Sonja Haynes Stone Center for Research in Black Culture and Hi
 story\, Brown Gallery and Hitchcock Room
SUMMARY:Jamaica Gilmer In Conversation With Dr. Jasmine Cobb
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/jamaica-gilmer-in-conversation
 -with-dr-jasmine-cobb
CATEGORIES:Lectures
END:VEVENT
