DESCRIPTION:The Right Kind of Jew:  Laura Z. Hobson’s Gentleman’s Agree
 ment and the Bargain\nof American Assimilation\n\n \n\nRachel Gordan\, Ass
 ociate Professor of Religion at the University of Florida\, revisits Laura
  Z. Hobson’s landmark 1947 novel Gentleman’s Agreement. Through Hobson
 ’s life and work\, Gordan explores the promises—and costs—of assimil
 ation and what it meant to become the “right kind” of Jew in twentieth
 -century America.
GEO:35.907852;-79.050272
LOCATION:The Sonja Haynes Stone Center for Research in Black Culture and Hi
 story\, Hitchcock room
SUMMARY:Kaplan Brauer Lecture: Rachel Gordan
