X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/community-stories-sustaining-north-carolinas-black-heritage"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261017T041253Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53138241993766
DTSTART:20261031T140000Z
DTEND:20261031T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:Community Stories: Sustaining North Carolina’s Black Heritage
  at the Gregg Museum of Art & Design presents a series of vignettes explor
 ing spaces of dignity\, belonging\, safety\, and imagination within Black 
 communities across North Carolina. Featuring historical photographs\, cont
 emporary images\, artworks from the Gregg Museum collection including a ha
 ndmade guitar by Freeman Vines\, and ephemera from community partners\, th
 e exhibition reflects on place\, memory\, creativity\, and spiritual resil
 ience across generations. Through stories of triumph and adversity\, Commu
 nity Stories honors the ways Black Americans have sustained and uplifted t
 heir communities through family\, entrepreneurship\, cultural expression\,
  and soulful imagination\, while inspiring future generations.
GEO:35.784925;-78.661662
LOCATION:Gregg Museum of Art & Design
SUMMARY:Community Stories: Sustaining North Carolina’s Black Heritage
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/community-stories-sustaining
 -north-carolinas-black-heritage
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/death-and-mourning-in-the-mountains-a-special-guided-tour-at-vance-birthplace"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261017T041253Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54195970974905
DTSTART:20261031T140000Z
DTEND:20261031T183000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us at Vance Birthplace on Saturday\, Oct. 31 for our new D
 eath and Mourning in the Mountains tour to learn how the culture around de
 ath and funerary practices changed throughout the 1800s. Led by site staff
 \, you’ll move through the historic grounds to explore how the Appalachi
 an climate and cultures of Western North Carolina as well as technological
  advances in the funeral industry shaped the end of life in the mountains.
 \n\nTours are offered at 10am and 1pm and will last approximately 90 minut
 es\, including an optional hike to the old Vance family cemetery. Tickets 
 cost $10.70 per person via Zeffy. Spots are limited\, so we recommend regi
 stering in advance. Join us to learn\, ask questions\, and connect with th
 e region’s history through this rarely discussed chapter of Appalachian 
 history.\n\nIf you have any questions\, please feel free to reach out to u
 s at vance@dncr.nc.gov or give us a call at (828) 645-6706!
GEO:35.700986;-82.496251
LOCATION:Governor Zebulon B. Vance Birthplace
SUMMARY:Death and Mourning in the Mountains: A Special Guided Tour at Vance
  Birthplace
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/death-and-mourning-in-the-mo
 untains-a-special-guided-tour-at-vance-birthplace
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Guided Tours
CATEGORIES:Special Site Programs
END:VEVENT
