DESCRIPTION:Join the Rural Interprofessional Longitudinal Scholars (RIPLS) 
 Program for a virtual public seminar exploring what it takes to build sust
 ainable practices in the health professions. \n\n \n\nThe RIPLS Program br
 ings together health professions students from UNC-Chapel Hill\, UNC Pembr
 oke\, and UNC Wilmington to collaborate\, learn\, and lead in rural health
  care settings. Through immersive experiences and ongoing interprofessiona
 l learning opportunities\, RIPLS prepares future health professionals to b
 etter understand rural communities and work collaboratively across discipl
 ines. \n\n \n\nQuirina Vallejos\, MPH\, Executive Director of NC Farmworke
 rs' project will lead an engaging discussion about migrant farmworker heal
 thcare in eastern North Carolina. \n\n \n\nStudents\, faculty\, staff\, co
 mmunity partners\, and health professionals are invited to attend this fre
 e virtual seminar.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Promoting Farmworker Access to Health Care Through a Network of Col
 laborations
