X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/history-for-lunch-the-role-of-baptisteries-in-byzantine-pilgrimage-sites-of-the-levant"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261017T041253Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53983015248310
DTSTART:20261104T170000Z
DTEND:20261104T180000Z
DESCRIPTION:Dr. Robert W. Smith\, the Distinguished Professor of History at
  Mid-Atlantic Christian University\, will take participants from modern ba
 ptismal practices of congregations in eastern North Carolina to Byzantine 
 baptisteries in the Holy Land. While modern Christians in the United State
 s may undergo multiple baptisms\, "rebaptism" was a capital offense under 
 the Law Code of the Byzantine Empire. This presentation will propose an ex
 planation for how the baptisteries of pilgrimage facilities functioned leg
 ally in the Levant. Dr. Smith has conducted archaeological excavations at 
 the ancient city of Abila\, Jordan\, since 1984\, including the city’s p
 ilgrimage complex.
GEO:36.296532;-76.219757
LOCATION:Museum of the Albemarle\, Gaither Auditorium
SUMMARY:History for Lunch: The Role of Baptisteries in Byzantine Pilgrimage
  Sites of the Levant
