DESCRIPTION:Shana Bushyhead Condill (Eastern Band of Cherokee Indians)\, Ex
 ecutive Director of the Museum of the Cherokee People\, and Andrew Denson\
 , professor of history at Western Carolina University\, will discuss the c
 hallenges involved in remembering the Revolution in the mountain region. I
 n particular\, they will examine the planning and creation of the Museum o
 f the Cherokee People’s current exhibition\, Unrelenting: Cherokee Peopl
 e and the American Revolution. The Friends of the Archives annual business
  meeting will follow the program at approximately 3 p.m.
