BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.unc.edu/event/the-ritual-of-belonging-35-years-of-the-friday-center"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20261017T041329Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54115387065565
DTSTART:20261105T233000Z
DTEND:20261106T014500Z
DESCRIPTION:Come. Connect. Celebrate.\n\n \n\nIn 1991\, UNC President Willi
 am C. Friday opened the doors to what he called "the citizens' classroom\,
 " a place built to make learning and connection open to everyone\, with or
  without a UNC degree. Named for Bill and Ida Friday\, two North Carolinia
 ns defined by their service to education and public life\, the Friday Cent
 er was founded on a simple belief: learning never stops.\n\nFor 35 years\,
  the Friday Center has carried that belief forward by opening doors\, brin
 ging people together\, and extending Carolina's knowledge beyond the tradi
 tional classroom. It is a place where the University and the community mee
 t\, where ideas are shared\, relationships are built\, and learning become
 s part of a larger public life.\n\nThis November\, we're celebrating 35 ye
 ars with an evening centered on something that has always been essential t
 o the Friday Center: the power of gathering\, and the belonging it creates
 .\n\nJoining us is Casper ter Kuile\, author of The Power of Ritual and co
 -founder of Sacred Design Lab.\n\n \n\nTHE POWER OF RITUAL\n\nAmidst risin
 g rates of disconnection\, what are the rituals that gather us together? H
 ow can we deepen our relationships\, make meaningful connections\, and exp
 erience joyful belonging? Join author and co-founder of Sacred Design Lab 
 Casper ter Kuile for an evening's conversation on the power of ritual. You
 'll explore how to cultivate the containers of connection at home\, on cam
 pus\, and in the wider community. Learn how ritual can weave us back into 
 a fabric of common life.\n\n \n\nThe Evening\n\n6:30pm | Director's recept
 ion\, join us for refreshments and conversation\n7:15pm | Casper's talk\, 
 followed by a live Q&A\n\n \n\nThis is a free event\, but space is limited
 \, and registration is required to attend.
GEO:35.899895;-79.012764
LOCATION:William and Ida Friday Center
SUMMARY:The Ritual of Belonging: 35 Years of the Friday Center
