BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/copy-of-deep-sky-astronomy-3512"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261017T041254Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51498196145905
DTSTART:20261107T230000Z
DTEND:20261108T010000Z
DESCRIPTION:This event is free to attend\, but registration is requested. \
 n\nJoin local astronomers with the Greensboro Astronomy Club as we observe
  the night skies over the Iron Ore Belt Access. Attendees may expect to se
 e closer-than-typical views of the moon\, planets\, star clusters\, and ot
 her celestial objects subject to change with time of year and local sky da
 rkness.\n\nTelescopes and viewing equipment will be set up on site but you
  may wish to bring your own binoculars or telescope\, plus a chair or blan
 ket for seating. Dress for the weather. Flashlights & headlamps should hav
 e a red-light option or filter to protect your night vision.\n\nSkywatchin
 g sessions may be cancelled at the last minute for weather. Please registe
 r at the Register link so you can be emailed in the event of cancellation.
 \n\nProgram equipment and instruction provided by members of the Greensbor
 o Astronomy Club\, which meet the third Friday of each month at the Greens
 boro Science Center. Learn more about their organization here: \n\nhttps:/
 /greensboroastronomyclub.org/\n\nStar-gazing Etiquette:\n\nPlease use a re
 d light at the observing session and keep any light pointed at the ground.
  As your eyes adapt\, a light is not needed at all.Pease do not touch any 
 telescopes or other equipment unless permission is given and form a orderl
 y line behind each telescope. Please do not allow children or pets to run 
 around the observing area. Pets must be on a leash no longer than 6 feet a
 t all times. This is to protect others' safety and the equipment.Stock pho
 to © Pexels / Lucas Pezeta
GEO:36.23742;-79.785591
LOCATION:Haw River State Park - Iron Ore Belt Access 
SUMMARY:Deep Sky Astronomy
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/copy-of-deep-sky-astronomy-3
 512
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.unc.edu/event/toshi-reagon-ecotones"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20261017T041329Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53682637377333
DTSTART:20261108T000000Z
DTEND:20261108T010000Z
DESCRIPTION:Some performances entertain. Others leave audiences seeing the 
 world differently. In EcoTones\, music\, storytelling\, research\, persona
 l history\, and lived experience come together in an experience that feels
  less like a performance and more like a gathering. Warm\, joyful\, and ch
 allenging\, the work invites audiences to consider what happens when diffe
 rent worlds meet and what becomes possible in the spaces between them.\n\n
  \n\nInspired by the ecological concept of an ecotone—the place where di
 stinct ecosystems overlap and create the conditions for new life—EcoTone
 s explores the intersections that shape our lives\, communities\, and futu
 res. The result is a shared act of discovery that reveals unexpected conne
 ctions and invites audiences to see familiar questions from new perspectiv
 es.\n\n \n\nCreated by Toshi Reagon in collaboration with UNC-Chapel Hill 
 scholars Danielle Spurlock and Danielle Purifoy and Durham-based writer\, 
 scholar\, and activist Alexis Pauline Gumbs\, the performance places artis
 ts and researchers side by side on stage. Their stories\, questions\, idea
 s\, and experiences become part of the work itself\, reflecting Toshi’s 
 belief that important voices and perspectives in our communities belong in
  shared public conversation.\n\n \n\nStudent tickets always $11. Eligible 
 for CLE. Find out more and buy tickets at: https://carolinaperformingarts.
 org/events/toshireagon-ecotones/
GEO:35.911208;-79.051989
LOCATION:Memorial Hall
SUMMARY:Toshi Reagon EcoTones
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/toshi-reagon-ecotones
CATEGORIES:Performances
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/ncma-educator-online-course-art-and-sel"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261017T041254Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53973578540735
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261108
DESCRIPTION:In this self-paced\, 15-hour course\, educators explore an arts
 -based approach to social emotional learning through themes of Mindfulness
 \, Identity\, Perspective Sharing\, Community Building\, and Agency. They 
 will participate in experiences that model growth and development of justi
 ce-oriented\, global citizens. A certificate of participation for 15 hours
  will be provided (1.5 CEU\, with approval from  the local school system).
  This course was developed in collaboration with the Friday Institute for 
 Educational Innovation. The course runs from October 6th - December 8th an
 d educators can join at any point. $18 Members\, $20 Nonmembers.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:NCMA Online Educator Course: Art and SEL
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/ncma-educator-online-course-
 art-and-sel
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Workshops & Trainings
END:VEVENT
