DESCRIPTION:The Stone Center’s Diaspora Festival of Black & Independent F
 ilm returns for another powerful celebration of cinema\, storytelling\, an
 d voices from across the African diaspora. Since 2004\, the festival has b
 rought audiences together for compelling films\, engaging conversations\, 
 and thought-provoking dialogue with filmmakers\, scholars\, and our commun
 ity.\n\n \n\nESEUSEU: THE ETERNAL SONG\nDir.: Zaya Benazzo\, Maurizio Bena
 zzo |Kenya\, United States | Doc | 61 MIN\nLand: Olosho le Maa (Kenya)\n\n
 \nThe Eternal Song: Eseuseu opens a portal into the ancestral wisdom and I
 ndigenous traditions of the Olosho le Maa community in Kenya\, calling us 
 to remember\, grieve\, heal\, and act.\n\n \n\nCome experience an unforget
 table evening of film and conversation. We can’t wait to see you there! 
 RSVP: https://go.unc.edu/filmfest2026
GEO:35.907852;-79.050272
LOCATION:The Sonja Haynes Stone Center for Research in Black Culture and Hi
 story\, Hitchcock Room
SUMMARY:Diaspora Festival of Black & Independent Film Screening 6
