DTSTAMP:20261017T041255Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54152808493946
DTSTART:20261115T200000Z
DTEND:20261115T220000Z
DESCRIPTION:*Registration required to reserve your spot* Follow the link ab
 ove to reserve your spot.        The registration link will be available s
 tarting 11/1/26.\n\nJoin a Lake James State Park Ranger for a boat tour on
  beautiful Lake James! Participants will enjoy approximately two hours on 
 the water while exploring key landmarks around the park\, and learning abo
 ut its fascinating history and natural resources. As we cruise along the s
 horeline\, we will keep our eyes open for wildlife\, waterfowl\, and Bald 
 Eagles. This will be an opportunity to experience Lake James State Park fr
 om a different perspective with a focus on the Paddy's Creek and Linville 
 River areas of the lake.\n\nMeeting Location: Lake James State Park Paddy'
 s Creek Access- East Shelter\nDuration: Approximately 2 hours 3:00PM-5:00P
 M\n\nPlease Bring: Personal floatation device(we can provide basic PFDs if
  needed)\, water\, sunglasses\, and a jacket \n\nThings to know: Participa
 nts may bring cameras or other items they feel will make them comfortable 
 but please pack light as space will be limited on the boat. Everybody must
  register prior to the event to have a spot on the boat. Registration is o
 nly for the name listed\, children or spouses have to register separately.
  Space is limited to 6 people. If you cannot make it please call us so we 
 can open the spot for another person.
GEO:35.760718;-81.882276
LOCATION:Lake James State Park - Paddy's Creek Access\, East Shelter
SUMMARY:An Evening on the Lake 
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/an-evening-on-the-lake-2150
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Guided Tours
CATEGORIES:Outdoor & Recreation
CATEGORIES:Nature & Wildlife Programs
CATEGORIES:Youth & Family Activities
END:VEVENT
