X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261017T041255Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53498826636173
DTSTART:20261121T160000Z
DTEND:20261121T180000Z
DESCRIPTION:Try your hand at artifact conservation! Help our archaeologists
  discover new finds by carefully excavating concretions to discover hidden
  artifacts. Kids will use a toothpick to carefully excavate chocolate chip
 s and candy pieces from a cookie\, giving them a “taste” of one step o
 f maritime artifact conservation. The best part: you can eat your finds! F
 or children ages 4 and up. \n\nCome by anytime between 11:00 a.m. and 1 p.
 m. to try cookie archaeology! This program is free and open to the public 
 and is sponsored by the Friends of the Graveyard of the Atlantic Museum. R
 eservations are not required. Call 252-986-0720 for more information.
GEO:35.206348;-75.704058
LOCATION:Graveyard of the Atlantic Museum
SUMMARY:Cookie Archaeology 
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/cookie-archaeology-2734
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/thanksgiving-culinary-cultural-history"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261017T041255Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54056088297899
DTSTART:20261121T160000Z
DTEND:20261121T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:Did you know that our modern Thanksgiving holiday largely has i
 ts origins in 1863? During the midst of the Civil War\, President Lincoln 
 proclaimed a day of Thanksgiving on the last Thursday of November to help 
 heal the wounds of the nation and to restore peace and union.\n\nLincoln u
 ltimately decided to make this Thanksgiving proclamation at the petition o
 f Sarah Josepha Hale\, editor of Godey's Lady's Book\, who had advocated f
 or such a holiday for over 15 years! This started an annual tradition whic
 h has been celebrated nationwide ever since.\n\nFor Lincoln and the loyal 
 states in 1863\, this Thanksgiving holiday allowed Americans to give thank
 s for major campaign victories (like Gettysburg) that year\, for continued
  union of the loyal states\, and blessings upon those who had lost loved o
 nes in the war.\n\n \n\nBennett Place invites you to join us in celebratin
 g & learning more about Thanksgiving with this special event on Saturday N
 ovember 21 from 11:00 - 3:00. Learn more about the holiday\, its Civil War
  roots\, women's history\, Indigenous foodways\, and the cultural dishes t
 hat flavored this all American celebration. Participate in our recipe exch
 ange (be sure to bring a hard copy of yours!)\, hearth cooking demonstrati
 ons\, crafts\, and historic games! Craft vendors will also be selling ware
 s.  We request a $10 donation for entrance to support the site\, however\,
  visitors may attend for free.
GEO:36.029293;-78.975047
LOCATION:Bennett Place State Historic Site
SUMMARY:Thanksgiving: Culinary & Cultural History
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/thanksgiving-culinary-cultur
 al-history
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Special Site Programs
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/copy-of-nc-the-beautiful-invasive-plant-purge-2268"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261017T041255Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53692514966869
DTSTART:20261121T170000Z
DTEND:20261121T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:“Invasive” plants are introduced\, aggressively-growing pla
 nts that negatively impact local ecosystems. Join park staff at Haw River 
 State Park’s Iron Ore Belt Access to help remove these leafy invaders! \
 n\nTypical workdays start with paperwork for new volunteers (less than fiv
 e minutes) followed by a short hike to the work area where volunteers will
  receive instruction on how to identify the target species of the day. The
  rest of the time will be used on employing hands-on\, seasonally appropri
 ate techniques to remove invasive plants from the landscape\, helping to r
 estore the area for native plants and wildlife. \n\nAdvance registration i
 s required as supplies and space are limited. This opportunity is only ope
 n to volunteers ages 12 and up. Any volunteers under the age of 16 must be
  registered with and accompanied by an adult. \n\nVolunteers should wear l
 ong sleeves\, long pants\, and close-toed shoes. Please bring work gloves 
 and loppers or pruning shears if you have them\, but if not they will be p
 rovided (and you don't need to let us know in advance either way). Meet at
  the parking lot of the Iron Ore Belt Access.
GEO:36.23742;-79.785591
LOCATION:Haw River State Park - Iron Ore Belt Access 
SUMMARY:NC the Beautiful: Invasive Plant Purge
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/copy-of-nc-the-beautiful-inv
 asive-plant-purge-2268
CATEGORIES:Organizational
CATEGORIES:Volunteer Opportunities
CATEGORIES:Outdoor & Recreation
CATEGORIES:Statewide Clean Up
END:VEVENT
