DTSTAMP:20261017T041256Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52569559741267
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270116
DESCRIPTION:This exhibit tells the stories of seven everyday North Carolini
 ans and extraordinary leaders — Gertrude Weil\, Henry Owl\, Joe Lewis\, 
 Abraham Galloway\, Ronald Mace\, James Hunter\, and Willa Player — who p
 etitioned\, protested\, and organized to expand democracy. The exhibit exp
 lores change\, freedom\, civic responsibility\, and overcoming challenges 
 by telling the story of a few North Carolinians who have raised their voic
 es to call out injustice and fully participate in our democratic society.
GEO:36.092774;-79.436435
LOCATION:May Memorial Library
SUMMARY:Making Our Voices Heard (America 250 NC Traveling Exhibit) 
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/making-our-voices-heard
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/mecklenburgs-declaration-ncs-revolutionary-presbyterians"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261017T041256Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53178468656742
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270116
DESCRIPTION:An article published in the April 30\, 1819 edition of the Rale
 igh Register and North Carolina Gazette proclaimed the following: “It is
  not probably known to many of our readers\, that the citizens of Mecklenb
 urg County\, in this State\, made a Declaration of Independence more than 
 a year before Congress made theirs. The following Document on the subject 
 has lately come to the hands of the Editor from unquestionable authority\,
   and is published that it may go down to posterity.”  \n\nThe document 
 in question was called the Mecklenburg Declaration of Independence\, and i
 t had allegedly declared Mecklenburg “free and independent” from Briti
 sh rule on May 20\, 1775. Of the 27 men who were said to have signed the d
 ocument\, almost all were Presbyterian.\n\nBut many people were confused 
 – why were they just now hearing about this revolutionary action? The or
 iginal document burned in a house fire in 1800\, and the published version
  had been reconstructed from notes made by the clerk of the 1775 meeting. 
 No extant copies could be found.\n\nThe debate over the authenticity of th
 e Mecklenburg Declaration began. And\, when a copy of a document called th
 e Mecklenburg Resolves written on May 30\, 1775\, was discovered in a 1775
  newspaper\, the debate intensified. The Resolves were revolutionary\, but
  stopped short of declaring independence. Did both documents exist? Or was
  the Declaration being conflated with the Resolves?\n\nExamine the evidenc
 e and decide for yourself by visiting the new exhibit\, “Mecklenburg Dec
 laration?” at the Presbyterian Heritage Center.\n\nThe PHC is open Tuesd
 ay-Friday (10-4) and Saturday (12-4).
GEO:35.646737;-82.300463
LOCATION:Presbyterian Heritage Center
SUMMARY:Mecklenburg's Declaration: NC's Revolutionary Presbyterians
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/mecklenburgs-declaration-ncs
 -revolutionary-presbyterians
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/mexicos-magical-migrations-institute"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261017T041256Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53320897836257
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270116
DESCRIPTION:Applications for the 2027 Mexico’s Magical Migrations Institu
 te are now closed. \n\nExperience one of the world’s greatest migrations
 : monarch butterflies on their wintering grounds.Observe humpback whale so
 cial interactions.Visit and learn about the Mazahua people at La Casa de l
 a Cultura Mazahua.Discover connections between Mexico and North Carolina.P
 articipating educators will witness two of nature’s greatest spectacles 
 – wintering monarch butterflies and humpback whales. Each year one of th
 e world’s greatest migrations takes place as millions of monarch butterf
 lies from the US and Canada travel south to the forested Mexican highlands
 . Once they arrive\, they begin a period of winter hibernation by clusteri
 ng together in huge numbers\, blanketing the surrounding vegetation. As th
 e butterflies are arriving in Mexico\, so are humpback whales. Concluding 
 their own incredible migration from their feeding waters off Alaska\, larg
 e numbers of humpback whales gather off Mexico’s Pacific coast. They com
 e to these warmer waters to breed and to give birth. Learn about these mag
 ical migrations from local experts and explore connections to North Caroli
 na. We will share our adventures with students at home through daily blog 
 posts from the field.\n\nDates: January 13-20\, 2027. (Mandatory pre- and 
 post-trip sessions will be held in Raleigh on Saturday\, December 5\, 2026
  and Saturday\, November 6\, 2027.)\n\nLocations: Toluca\, Macho de Agua\,
  and Puerto Vallarta\, Mexico and Raleigh\, N.C.\n\nGroup Size: Limited to
  12 participants. (Note: We anticipate that Mexican teachers will join wit
 h American educators to form an international team.)\n\nActivity Level: Mo
 derate to rigorous including hiking (up to 2 miles) on uneven terrain\, wa
 lking at high altitudes (~10\,000 ft)\, and riding horses on trails with a
  guide.\n\nCost: $2200*\nIncludes round-trip airfare from Raleigh to Mexic
 o\, in-country transportation\, instruction\, lodging\, and meals. Partici
 pants will be responsible for travel to and from Raleigh and expenses in R
 aleigh during pre- and post-trip sessions. See below for scholarship oppor
 tunities.\n\n*The cost of all Institutes are significantly reduced thanks 
 the generous support of the Friends of the Museum and the Goodnight Educat
 ional Foundation. Teachers that apply and are selected from the list of ea
 stern counties (see below for details) may be eligible to receive a Simple
  Gifts Scholarship\, which is provided through the generous support of the
  Simple Gifts Fund and the Anonymous Trust. \n \n\nApplications for Mexico
 ’s Magical Migrations 2027 Institute are now closed. The application dea
 dline was Monday\, October 12\, 2026.\n\nApplications for Summer 2027 Inst
 itutes (Yellowstone and Blue Ridge) will open in November 2026.
LOCATION:Toluca\, Macho de Agua\, and Puerto Vallarta\, Mexico and Raleigh\
 , N.C.
SUMMARY:Sold Out: Mexico’s Magical Migrations Institute
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/mexicos-magical-migrations-i
 nstitute
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Workshops & Trainings
END:VEVENT
