BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.unc.edu/event/designing-ai-assisted-qualitative-research-workflows-2658"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20261017T041330Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54230893358451
DTSTART:20270210T140000Z
DTEND:20270210T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:This workshop will introduce participants to a framework for co
 nsidering the consequences of using generative AI in qualitative research 
 designs and workflows (Paulus\, 2023\; Paulus & Lester\, 2024). We will st
 art by defining digital research workflows and how to engage in technologi
 cal reflexivity throughout the design process. We will learn how to distin
 guish between methodological strategies and technological tactics\, i.e. w
 hy researchers must first know what they want to do before choosing the be
 st tools for doing it (Woolf & Silver\, 2018). We will then discuss the ge
 nres of AI-assist technologies currently available to qualitative research
 ers and how to select the most appropriate platform.\n\n \n\nMAXQDA AI-Ass
 ist tools will be used to illustrate tactics currently available to resear
 chers. Next we will consider the consequences of AI-Assisted workflows\, a
 cknowledging dilemmas such as how generative AI is challenging the essence
  of what it means to do qualitative work (Paulus & Marone\, 2025\; Paulus\
 , Lester & Davis\, 2026). Finally\, we will discuss best practices for how
  to transparently report and evaluate researcher use of AI (Lester & Paulu
 s\, 2026). Workshop time will alternate between short lectures and demonst
 rations and small-group discussion and application activities.\n\n \n\nReg
 istration and fee (refundable for UNCCH students) are required. This event
  is sponsored by the UNC Odum Institute for Research.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Designing AI-Assisted Qualitative Research Workflows
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/designing-ai-assisted-qualitat
 ive-research-workflows-2658
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
