X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/temple-theatre-presents-red-white-temple-patriotic-revue-21"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261017T041257Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54239730869277
DTSTART:20270304T190000Z
DTEND:20270304T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:Temple Theatre is one of North Carolina's premier regional thea
 tres\, offering Broadway-quality productions in the heart of downtown Sanf
 ord. \n\nExperience the heart and soul of America in Temple’s high-energ
 y patriotic musical revue that celebrates the nation’s heritage through 
 song\, dance\, and spirited storytelling. With a mix of humor\, history\, 
 and heart this revue is a foot-stomping-flag-waving celebration designed t
 o ignite pride in audiences of every generation.\n\nTickets range from $25
  to $40 with discounts available for active military\, Lee County educator
 s and students\, and groups of 10 or more. Visit templeshows.org or call 9
 19-774-4512 for more information.
GEO:35.48114;-79.178793
LOCATION:Temple Theatre
SUMMARY:Temple Theatre Presents: "Red\, White\, & Temple Patriotic Revue"
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/temple-theatre-presents-red-
 white-temple-patriotic-revue-21
CATEGORIES:Performances & Arts
CATEGORIES:Theater & Musicals
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.unc.edu/event/the-surge-an-ode-to-sinead-oconnor"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20261017T041330Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53682686405017
DTSTART:20270305T000000Z
DTEND:20270305T010000Z
DESCRIPTION:For anyone who has ever questioned their place\, pushed against
  expectations\, or wondered what it costs to remain true to yourself\, The
  Surge: An Ode to Sinéad O’Connor is for you.\n\nInspired by the music\
 , words\, and enduring spirit of Sinéad O’Connor\, director and choreog
 rapher Sonya Tayeh creates a powerful dance experience performed by ten wo
 men over the age of 40. O’Connor’s music and narration\, drawn from he
 r memoir Rememberings\, weave throughout the performance. \n\n \n\nThe Sur
 ge is a reflection on identity\, aging\, freedom\, and the courage require
 d to live authentically in a world that often rewards conformity. What eme
 rges is both deeply personal and unexpectedly communal: a celebration of w
 omen who refuse to disappear\, soften themselves for others\, or surrender
  the right to define their own lives.\n\n \n\nStudent tickets always $11. 
 Eligible for CLE. Find out more and buy tickets at: https://carolinaperfor
 mingarts.org/events/the-surge/
GEO:35.911208;-79.051989
LOCATION:Memorial Hall
SUMMARY:The Surge: An Ode to Sinéad O’Connor
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/the-surge-an-ode-to-sinead-oco
 nnor
CATEGORIES:Performances
END:VEVENT
